{"id": "EUVD-2026-76622", "enisaUuid": "f966ae34-c3d2-361b-af91-5a95e6ab006c", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nNFSv4.1: fix layout segment leak on the pnfs_layout_process() forget path\n\nWhen the server returns a new layout stateid while a valid one is still\nheld, pnfs_layout_process() calls pnfs_mark_matching_lsegs_return() on\nthe on-stack free_me list and jumps to out_forget. Segments whose\nreference count drops to zero are unlinked from lo->plh_segs and moved\nto free_me by mark_lseg_invalid(); for an idle cached segment the layout\nheader holds the only reference, so this happens on the first decrement.\n\nout_forget never drains free_me -- only the success path calls\npnfs_free_lseg_list().\n\nCommit 814b84971388 (\"pNFS/NFSv4: Fix a layout segment leak in\npnfs_layout_process()\") added the drain; commit 08bd8dbe8882\n(\"pNFS/NFSv4: Try to return invalid layout in pnfs_layout_process()\")\nremoved it while switching the destination to lo->plh_return_segs, which\nis drained elsewhere. Commit fb700ef02676 (\"NFSv4.1: Simplify layout\nreturn in pnfs_layout_process()\") switched the destination back to\nfree_me without restoring the drain.\n\nRestore the pnfs_free_lseg_list() call.", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:46:25", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:51:23", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f52188118d319b47d49ee91a897f6afda4879c59", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ad3e41855325e55623276660ef20fbc3b8ba087f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a080bb69d30f11738d753a60d1eb733d627c2093", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7c5b0e813efd9124760d5fd1bfc6b229f03fb1a2", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/36e3f13bf0728f4ce11ee8904cec82a783222f62", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/32ac1b0b7f1cfa0d1a1faf9c72f4154046101070", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ee5a386cfe60f3f8286de16a9db8e1a08f0bc124"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-89710", "GHSA-84pc-7mxq-h2j8"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "11e5b08d-c138-378e-b03c-664916a59777", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "1fe35dd7-8243-3da9-a744-5c298aeb089f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.221"}, {"id": "47b3c0fb-9a9e-303e-bee3-35b378b483c3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "fb700ef026766c95578aafc0db1b208946e7ad4f <ee5a386cfe60f3f8286de16a9db8e1a08f0bc124"}, {"id": "544ee471-18a3-3b17-b09c-ae7b4b85534a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.4"}, {"id": "6d69913e-2750-3a07-a47c-ce0269e7e8af", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "fb700ef026766c95578aafc0db1b208946e7ad4f <ad3e41855325e55623276660ef20fbc3b8ba087f"}, {"id": "6e6cdb67-82a6-37a8-bc7a-3e171158b3e1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "7c2fc9c0-6f16-31af-961b-b8aaa929d753", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.109"}, {"id": "882372ce-720a-3164-9240-0dc661311fbc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.157"}, {"id": "961dc173-07a3-3ff5-a9d9-dac7ef03f0f1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.188"}, {"id": "a3e77472-fa09-3af5-9cf2-6e860b63d40c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "fb700ef026766c95578aafc0db1b208946e7ad4f <32ac1b0b7f1cfa0d1a1faf9c72f4154046101070"}, {"id": "ac40fdaa-aae9-334f-b6a0-649233e5df9c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "fb700ef026766c95578aafc0db1b208946e7ad4f <7c5b0e813efd9124760d5fd1bfc6b229f03fb1a2"}, {"id": "b300d98d-7275-3b06-8ebf-b66892eb553d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "fb700ef02676